# A name the checker was told about and the engines never learned (roadmap Gap R.136, ADR 0264's sweep).
#
# `predeclared.go` keeps one list of the names the checker is allowed to see. Ten of them are in that list
# and callable on neither engine: `map`, `filter`, `isinstance`, `hash`, `id`, `getattr`, `callable`,
# `pow`, `divmod`, `fabs`. The row this probe pins is the same shape `floor` / `ceil` / `sqrt` had until
# ADR 0264 — the toolchain accepts a program, and then the engine refuses to run it — measured by walking
# the predeclared table and calling every name in it.
#
# `pow` is the sharpest of the ten because CPython runs it in one line:
#
#     print(pow(2, 3))     # CPython 8 · --interp NameError, exit 3 · --aot exit 1 `unsupported call "pow"`
#
# so one leg spends a runtime trap and the other spends exit 1 — the contract's "your program has a
# compile error" class — on a program the reference evaluates without complaint (ADR 0211, L11.8). The
# fix is the one ADR 0264 made for the other three: implement it on both paths, or take the name out of
# the table so the checker stops promising it.
print(pow(2, 3))
